   "definition_quote": "We consider a sequential deferral problem over a known horizon $T$. ... the decision maker, who observes the self-confidence level $J_t$ ... either accepts the LLM answer or defers the query to a queue served by a pool of experts ... The cost incurred at round $t$ is $c_t:= c_{\\mathrm{hold}} B_t+ c_{\\mathrm{exp}} A_t+ c_e(1-A_t)(1-Y_t)$ ... The resulting problem is a finite-horizon Markov decision process (MDP)"
